  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1258 AM MDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nThe passing system will push east of us by Monday afternoon, leading \nto warmer and drier conditions across the region for the rest of the \nweek. High temperatures will climb into the 60s to low-70s, with \nmild overnight lows in the 30s-40s for the plains and 20s for the \nvalleys.\n\nOur next pattern change will come late this week, most likely Friday \nand into next weekend. Guidance shows a broad upper trough deepening \nover the Pacific Northwest, with southwest flow moving into our \narea. This should help return moisture to the mountains, potential \nspreading more widespread rain into the region over the weekend. As \nof now, this system also appears to bring some colder air with it, \nmeaning that the mountains at least may see more snow.",
